---
import Base from "@Layout/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	Title="FLAVORS // APHRODITE"
	Description="The Aphrodite roadmap: a native Hermes plugin today, the standalone proxy for any OpenAI-compatible client, and the embedded Headroom core that keeps the engine portable."
>
	<main
		class="relative z-10 mx-auto flex w-full max-w-[1440px] flex-col gap-24 px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 lg:gap-32 lg:px-14 lg:py-28"
	>
		<!-- HERO -->
		<header class="relative flex w-full flex-col items-start">
			<div
				class="mb-4 -rotate-1 border border-black bg-raw-blood px-3 py-1 text-[11px] font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-bone-white shadow-[3px_3px_0px_#000]"
			>
				FLAVORS // THE ROADMAP
			</div>
			<h1
				class="font-headline text-3xl font-black uppercase tracking-tight text-bone-white drop-shadow-[4px_4px_0px_#520612] sm:text-5xl"
			>
				One engine, many hosts
			</h1>
			<p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-bone-newsprint">
				Aphrodite's compression engine does not belong to one agent. The native Hermes
				plugin is the flagship flavor today - the deepest integration, the most
				capabilities - but the same CCR core runs standalone for any OpenAI-compatible
				client, and the engine's core is an embedded fork built to stay portable.
			</p>
			<div class="mt-6 flex max-w-4xl flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
				<span
					class="-rotate-2 border-2 border-black bg-raw-blood px-4 py-1.5 font-mono text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-bone-white shadow-[4px_4px_0px_#000]"
				>
					HERMES PLUGIN // TODAY
				</span>
				<span
					class="rotate-1 border-2 border-black bg-carbon-void px-4 py-1.5 font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-weathered-teal shadow-[4px_4px_0px_#000]"
				>
					STANDALONE PROXY // SHIPS TODAY
				</span>
				<span
					class="rotate-2 border-2 border-black bg-stamped-canary px-4 py-1.5 font-mono text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-soot-black shadow-[4px_4px_0px_#000]"
				>
					MORE HOSTS // PLANNED
				</span>
			</div>
		</header>

		<!-- FLAVOR: HERMES -->
		<section class="relative w-full">
			<div
				class="zine-box-crimson relative -rotate-[1.4deg] border-4 border-blood-crimson bg-carbon-void p-6 transition-transform duration-300 hover:rotate-0 sm:p-8"
			>
				<div
					class="absolute -top-3.5 left-6 border border-black bg-raw-blood px-3 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-bone-white shadow-[2px_2px_0px_#000]"
				>
					FLAVOR 01 // HERMES PLUGIN
				</div>
				<h2 class="mb-3 mt-2 font-headline text-lg font-black uppercase text-bone-white sm:text-xl">
					The full integration
				</h2>
				<p class="mb-3 font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-bone-newsprint">
					Six hooks, thirteen tools, the context engine, auto-launched dual proxies - the
					native flavor sees everything the agent sees. This is the flavor this site
					documents.
				</p>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
					<span class="border border-oxblood-dark bg-soot-black px-3 py-1 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase text-bone-newsprint">6 HOOKS</span>
					<span class="border border-oxblood-dark bg-soot-black px-3 py-1 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase text-bone-newsprint">13 TOOLS</span>
					<span class="border border-oxblood-dark bg-soot-black px-3 py-1 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase text-bone-newsprint">CONTEXT ENGINE</span>
					<span class="border border-oxblood-dark bg-soot-black px-3 py-1 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase text-bone-newsprint">DIRECTIVES</span>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- FLAVOR: STANDALONE PROXY -->
		<section class="relative w-full lg:w-10/12 lg:self-end">
			<div
				class="zine-box-crimson relative rotate-[1.4deg] border-4 border-blood-crimson bg-carbon-void p-6 transition-transform duration-300 hover:rotate-0 sm:p-8"
			>
				<div
					class="absolute -top-3.5 right-6 border border-black bg-weathered-teal px-3 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-bone-white shadow-[2px_2px_0px_#000]"
				>
					FLAVOR 02 // STANDALONE PROXY
				</div>
				<h2 class="mb-3 mt-2 font-headline text-lg font-black uppercase text-bone-white sm:text-xl">
					Any OpenAI-compatible client
				</h2>
				<p class="mb-3 font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-bone-newsprint">
					Point <code class="font-mono text-xs text-weathered-teal">base_url</code> at
					<code class="font-mono text-xs text-weathered-teal">:9798</code> (or
					<code class="font-mono text-xs text-weathered-teal">:9797</code>) and the same
					compression engine sits between the client and its LLM - token and cache
					listeners, SQLite or in-memory storage. What it cannot do is see inside the
					agent: no hook interception, no tools, no prompt injection.
				</p>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
					<span class="border border-oxblood-dark bg-soot-black px-3 py-1 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase text-bone-newsprint">OPENAI-COMPATIBLE</span>
					<span class="border border-oxblood-dark bg-soot-black px-3 py-1 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase text-bone-newsprint">TOKEN :9798</span>
					<span class="border border-oxblood-dark bg-soot-black px-3 py-1 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase text-bone-newsprint">CACHE :9797</span>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- PORTABILITY: HEADROOM CORE -->
		<section class="relative w-full">
			<div
				class="zine-box-crimson relative -rotate-[1.2deg] border-4 border-blood-crimson bg-carbon-void p-6 transition-transform duration-300 hover:rotate-0 sm:p-8"
			>
				<div
					class="absolute -top-3.5 left-6 border border-black bg-stamped-canary px-3 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-soot-black shadow-[2px_2px_0px_#000]"
				>
					FOUNDATION // EMBEDDED HEADROOM
				</div>
				<h2 class="mb-3 mt-2 font-headline text-lg font-black uppercase text-bone-white sm:text-xl">
					The portable core
				</h2>
				<p class="font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-bone-newsprint">
					Aphrodite embeds Headroom - a custom fork, tracked as a git submodule - as its
					content-transform core: the classifier, the smart crusher, the tokenizer. The
					Hermes-specific layer is a thin bridge on top. That separation is what makes
					new host flavors possible: the engine already speaks in content types and
					previews, not in agent APIs.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- ROADMAP NOTE -->
		<section class="relative w-full lg:w-9/12 lg:self-end">
			<div
				class="zine-box-subtle relative rotate-[1.6deg] border-[3px] border-zinc-dust/40 bg-carbon-void p-6 transition-transform duration-300 hover:rotate-0 sm:p-8"
			>
				<div
					class="absolute -top-3.5 right-6 border border-black bg-bone-newsprint px-3 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-soot-black shadow-[2px_2px_0px_#000]"
				>
					ROADMAP // PLANNED
				</div>
				<h2 class="mb-3 mt-2 font-headline text-lg font-black uppercase text-bone-white sm:text-xl">
					Other agents
				</h2>
				<p class="font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-bone-newsprint">
					Beyond Hermes, additional host flavors are planned - the standalone proxy path
					already works with any OpenAI-compatible agent today, and deeper native
					integrations follow the same hook-and-tool pattern the Hermes plugin
					established. No dates are promised on this page; when a new flavor ships, it is
					documented here.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- FOOTER -->
		<footer
			class="flex flex-col items-center justify-between gap-4 border-t-2 border-oxblood-dark pb-6 pt-12 text-xs text-zinc-dust sm:flex-row"
		>
			<div class="flex items-center gap-2">
				<span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 bg-raw-blood"></span>
				<span class="font-bold tracking-widest text-bone-white uppercase">APHRODITE CCR CORE</span>
			</div>
			<div class="flex items-center gap-4">
				<a class="transition-colors hover:text-bone-white" href="/plugin/">PLUGIN</a>
				<a class="transition-colors hover:text-bone-white" href="/hermes/">HERMES</a>
				<a class="transition-colors hover:text-bone-white" href="/setup/">SETUP</a>
				<span class="font-bold text-stamped-canary">CC0-1.0</span>
			</div>
		</footer>
	</main>
</Base>
